hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer a question  from one of my readers Jackie who is an  entrepreneur who has connections in  China with manufacturing companies so  he's in China and he wants to create  handbags and export them to the United  States Canada Australia and other  markets so he's asking for my advice on  how to find people to partner with in  those markets be able to sell his  products so it's a great opportunity  Jackie from talking to Canadian  entrepreneurs is a Canadians perspective  there's a number of companies who work  with Chinese manufacturers and have  difficulty with timelines and managing  the culture differences so if you were  running a professional operation and can  help kind of smooth those relations then  it could be a really good opportunity if  you're looking at partnering up I would  suggest trying to find a company who's  already in the business of selling  handbags so either look for somebody  who's creating their own handbags and  may not be happy with their provider  their supplier it could be an  opportunity for you to come in and maybe  start with a small project and expand  from there or look for somebody who's  already in the business maybe selling it  in the retail operation selling other  bags and are looking to potentially  create their own and that could be an  opportunity to come in and help them  with that product line I think that's  probably the best option instead of  looking for a new designer or a startup  company you ideally want somebody who  already has a way to sell the product so  they have a customer base it makes their  chance at success a lot higher and your  chance at success a lot higher you could  gamble on a start-up but the chances of  them being successful are pretty low  compared to someone who already has an  established customer base so I try to  reach out to those companies do some  research find some of those companies  introduce yourself start with some  samples start with a small project  hopefully it works out you can build the  relationship and move on to bigger and  bigger products so I hope that helps  Jackie for everybody else if you enjoyed  the video please give it a thumbs up I  always love seeing your thumbs ups and  if you also want to leave some feedback  on what you thought about the video as a  comment I'd love to hear from you as  well stay tuned and I will see in the  next episode  you
 

